menu "Boot Security Policy"

config BOOT_PRODUCTION
    bool "Production secure-boot policy"
    default n
    select BOOT_REQUIRE_SIGNATURE
    help
      Enable the fail-closed production policy for every image in the boot
      chain. The product loader must provide common/boot_security.cc with an
      audited P-256 verifier and an OTP-backed monotonic security-version
      provider. The preloader also consumes this symbol so that it cannot
      execute an unauthenticated field-upgrade loader in production.

config BOOT_MIN_SECURITY_VERSION
    int "Development minimum firmware security version"
    default 0
    range 0 2147483647
    depends on !BOOT_PRODUCTION
    help
      Development-only compile-time rollback floor. Production builds must
      read the floor from one-time-programmable or equivalently protected
      monotonic storage.

config BOOT_REQUIRE_SIGNATURE
    bool "Require ECDSA-P256 image signature"
    default n
    help
      Fail closed unless the product supplies verify_image_signature(). A
      production build selects this option automatically.

endmenu
